 3. 🛢️ 65 billion-barrel deal 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Via Truth Social

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The U.S. has struck a deal with Venezuela to take control of oil fields with 65 billion barrels of reserves, President Trump said on Truth Social yesterday.

 Why it matters: The unprecedented deal vastly increases U.S. energy security and dominance in the Western Hemisphere, reports Axios' Marc Caputo, who scooped Thursday that the deal was likely. 🔎 Zoom in: The details have yet to be released. But a source described the unorthodox arrangement as a type of "public-private partnership" between the U.S., private companies and Venezuela.

 "It's not a purchase," a U.S. government source said. "They're giving us equity. It's a type of corporate transaction where the U.S. has equity in the companies." The U.S. would have access to what's called "off-take oil," a guaranteed amount of crude that would be exchanged at cost, the source said. Keep reading . 

 
 
