 4. 🏡 Teetering housing market 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Redfin . Chart: Emily Peck/Axios The housing market has been in a low-boil recession for four years now, with anemic sales and the appearance of high prices, somehow without tanking the overall economy, Axios' Emily Peck reports. 

 Why it matters: Homeownership is the bedrock of the economy — it's how most Americans build wealth — and changes in the residential real estate market ripple out into things like consumer spending, the job market and inflation. Zoom in: Home sales are at levels last seen when the country was crawling out of a housing crisis more than a decade ago.

 Many homeowners don't want to give up their low mortgage rates and buy something else. Others are discouraged by the prospect of high mortgage rates and house prices that, in many markets, still hover at record highs. Keep reading . 

 
 
