 8. 🦋 1 for the road: Dolly International 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Empire State Building was lit in pink in tribute to Dolly Parton. Photo: Jeenah Moon/Reuters A push by fans to rename Nashville's airport for Dolly Parton is taking off.

 Tennessee Gov. Bill Lee and the CEO of the Metropolitan Nashville Airport Authority both came out in favor of the name change yesterday. It's expected to come up at the authority's meeting next month, AP reports . Catch up quick: Long before 80-year-old Parton died Tuesday, fans in January 2025 started an online petition calling for officials to rename Nashville International Airport in her honor. It got renewed attention following Parton's death, jumping to more than 164,000 signatures and counting.

 The change would make Parton the first woman whose name adorns one of America's 50 busiest airports. More from Axios Nashville . 

 
 
